Native Linux compiler workflow

The compiler, Ezero frontend/runtime, builder, integrator, verifier and text
codec are original Zero/Ezero code. Linux tools are native ELF programs.

Compose and build from canonical sources:
  zero-integrate PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_KERNEL.zero
  zero-build PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY NEW_KERNEL.zero
Run the native source/file checks:
  zero-check PROJECT_DIRECTORY NEW_TEST_DIRECTORY
The native programs refuse existing output paths. The builder validates the
compiler fixed point before emitting artifacts. No foreign-language project
script or interpreter is required by this workflow.

The same authored sources also build native Windows PE tools. Compiler CLI
companion libraries must remain adjacent to zero/ezero as documented in
tools/compiler-cli.ztext. See tools/build.ztext for exact output layout.

The current host checks do not claim a fresh Debian/Arch distribution or
independent kernel boot. Historical distribution observations, where retained,
apply only to their recorded versions. A platform matrix must identify the
actual executed userspace/kernel and tool hashes before being called current.
Use checks/README.ztext for the current verifier contract and limitations.
